{
  "_about": [
    "Answer key for the quality check (scripts/quality-check.js). Never copied into the scratch project.",
    "Paths are as they appear in the scratch project, after the runner's renames (dot-claude -> .claude, *.fixture -> *).",
    "A finding catches a bug when its file is one of `files` (or it names no file, or a URL, and `fileless` is true) and its",
    "text satisfies `match`: a list of alternatives, each a list of case-insensitive regexes that must ALL match. The text is",
    "the finding's what, context, fix, key, attachments and receipt (raw JSONL), or its report lines with the Receipt row",
    "(survivors). Findings are written in plain words with no code names (finding-contract.md), so each alternative names",
    "the consequence as a reader would say it; mechanism words usually appear only in the receipt.",
    "`lines` documents where each bug sits (the tests check it still does). With `lineMatch` true a finding inside a window",
    "(widened by 1 line) also counts; every bug here leaves it false, because the first live run showed a different finding",
    "on the same lines (a crash on a malformed URL, stale search results) being credited by line alone."
  ],
